{"c":[{"id":"f48370a3611e6add","sum":"B24, I2-I3, W3: person-details fill = 4 Jev calls; Groq 429s; TextEdit opens files from its Containers tmp; <select> is a hand-off; memory.ndjson = helper golden; unrestorable clipboard blocks paste; page snapshot mirrors Chrome AX; Helium NMH dir; page.sock proofs bind pid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"8d81c7b9a87754a7","sum":"B24, I3: person-details fill = 4 Jev calls (PER_FILL); Groq 429s, space writer calls 30 s; TextEdit opens files only from its Containers tmp; native <select> is a value-less hand-off; host memory.ndjson = helper golden, find lines by id.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"d32f644355f794d8","sum":"B24: a person-details fill asks twice (whose, then values): 4 Jev calls, PER_FILL in counting tests; Groq qwen3.8 429s within ~20 plans, space writer calls 30 s; sandboxed TextEdit opens files only from its Containers tmp.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-05aef102d22989aa","text":"B24: fill asks in two stages when a field takes a person's details (whose first, then values), so a fill is 4 Jev calls, not 2; tests that count calls use PER_FILL. Groq's qwen3.8 hits 429 token limits within ~20 plans; space writer calls 30 s.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T192504Z-2947a2d88b908a7e","text":"B24: TextEdit is sandboxed: a file named on its command line opens only from inside ~/Library/Containers/com.apple.TextEdit/Data/tmp (realfill-capture.ts makes its own folder there and deletes it).","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e9b74ce9f7778aba","sum":"B24, I3: Chrome AX shows a native <select> as AXPopUpButton with only the chosen option, so fill hands selects off with no value; host Fixtures/memory.ndjson is the helper golden byte for byte; tests find lines by id, never index.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T192504Z-d09a0e8b1bd722e1","text":"B24: Chrome's AX shows a native <select> as AXPopUpButton whose only child is the selected option; the option list is not readable without opening it, so fill names selects as hand-offs with no value (capture-2 probe).","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195224Z-8ef6ab64ee3f2dea","text":"I3: apps/caret Fixtures/memory.ndjson is the helper's golden byte for byte as of H1 (host-memory-5 request added, A16's wrote line is host-memory-9, no -8); tests find lines by id, never by index.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"3093b549fb68152a","sum":"I2-I3, W3: paste refused for unrestorable clipboard types; page-link snapshot mirrors Chrome AX; Helium reads NMH manifests from its --user-data-dir; page.sock proofs bind the helper pid.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"787299ed8ad30f01","sum":"I2-I3: paste route refused when the prior clipboard holds a type outside restorableTypes (AX write, else clipboardUnrestorable); page-link toWindowSnapshot must mirror Chrome AX (AXTimeField, radios under an AXGroup per name, select options as AXMenuItem).","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T195224Z-99ff86984f364892","text":"I3: host refuses the paste route when the prior clipboard holds a type outside ReconcilingClipboard.restorableTypes (file URL, private types): AX write instead, else fail clipboardUnrestorable. A17's VM probe lost a file-url item 5/5 while restore said restored.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T195842Z-c30fb40a821e024f","text":"I2: page-link.ts toWindowSnapshot must match Chrome AX for fill/controls.ts: time is AXTimeField, radios sit under an AXGroup per name attribute, select options are AXMenuItem children. PageControl has no fieldset legend, so page radio groups have no label.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"13ae7e710e2343cf","sum":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp --user-data-dir and reads NMH manifests from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts; both page.sock proofs (bridgeProof too) bind the helper pid, or a socket swap keeps the host's session.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-5a96910dba2d6b69","text":"W3: Helium 0.18 loads --load-extension on a temp --user-data-dir and reads Native Messaging manifests from <user-data-dir>/NativeMessagingHosts (accept.ts --browser passes 42/42); its Web Store page offers Add to Helium.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-74ab7d13fad22cf2","text":"W3: page.sock proofs both bind the helper pid (bridgeProof too), or a same-user process that swaps the socket path can pass the host's hello to the real helper and keep that session.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"07a41b3f18dd2c1e","sum":"W3/memory: bridge->host via XPC only; accept.ts needs --sign-identity, runs a temp launchd host; headless CfT focus sticks to CDP windows; XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; memory .md grants no authority (sqlite rules);   escapes for oxc; push v2/* to sam.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"eddb660e4954b5f4","sum":"W3, memory: bridge reaches the host over XPC only; accept.ts needs --sign-identity and runs a temp launchd host; headless CfT focus sticks to CDP windows; XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; memory markdown goes to the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"94d9cdb89929ed3f","sum":"W3: caret-bridge reaches the host over XPC, never page.sock; accept.ts needs --sign-identity (and --other-identity) and boots out its temp launchd host; headless CfT focuses a CDP-created window and activateTarget won't move it back.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-903b513efe20fc90","text":"W3: caret-bridge reaches the Caret host over XPC (CaretBridgeXPC), never page.sock; no <sock>.key exists. accept.ts needs --sign-identity <team SHA-1> (and --other-identity for refusal checks) and runs caret-bridge-testhost as a temporary launchd job it boots out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204321Z-98052ff285eab267","text":"W3: headless Chrome for Testing gives focus to a window CDP Target.createTarget opens and Target.activateTarget does not move it back; chrome.windows focused is reported in headless. Page window focus = active tab of the focused, last-focused window.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"569740c12f8fdab5","sum":"W3, memory: a client's setCodeSigningRequirement guards replies, not its first send, so XPCHostLink sends nothing before a verified reply; personal memory is markdown in <dir>/Memory, the real folder only without --data-dir.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204321Z-a08d2817ff5ece3d","text":"W3: NSXPCConnection.setCodeSigningRequirement on the client blocks what it receives, not its own first call; whoever owns the Mach name sees open's arguments, so XPCHostLink sends nothing until a verified reply.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204904Z-98cc6d5ebfceb30a","text":"Personal memory is markdown (helper/src/memory): MemoryStore(dir) keeps it in <dir>/Memory unless told otherwise, and main.ts uses ~/Library/Application Support/Caret/Memory only when --data-dir is not given, so tests and evals never open the real folder.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"4ac352ed8f3af9fe","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (state stays in memory.sqlite; fileDigest catches offline edits); write \\u2028 escapes for oxc; push v2/* to remote sam, never origin; B25: Ask on INTENT_ROUTE gpt-oss-120b, plans on WRITER_ROUTE qwen3.8 (Groq daily cap).","tree":{"c":[{"id":"6e639a4926698b7e","sum":"Memory markdown grants no authority (permissions, onItsOwn, clean runs stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill file puts it back on Tab; fileDigest catches offline edits). vite's oxc rejects a raw U+2028/U+2029 in a regex literal: write the escape.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T204920Z-024f4219fb18c6cf","text":"Memory markdown grants no authority: permissions and a skill's onItsOwn, clean runs and hand-off stay in memory.sqlite; editing a skill's file puts it back on Tab, and SkillJson.fileDigest catches edits made while Caret was stopped.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T204920Z-0ba29fff62387456","text":"vite's oxc parser rejects a regex literal holding a raw U+2028/U+2029 (a line terminator); write the \\u2028 escape. An agent's Write tool can turn the escape into the raw character.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e2ebd6c0099fdfde","sum":"Push v2/* to remote sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret); origin is the team hackathon repo. B25: Ask intents use INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plans WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8); qwen3.8's Groq 200k tokens/day runs out in dev; gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T210855Z-22a0908ac8155d26","text":"Push v2/* branches to the remote named sam (SamGu-NRX/Caret), where their PRs live. origin is the team hackathon repo (theodorexli/hackathon-2026-09-19); a bare 'git push origin' publishes there.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T211051Z-2bd567d78f578d5c","text":"B25: Ask intents go to INTENT_ROUTE (gpt-oss-120b), plan programs to WRITER_ROUTE (qwen3.8); qwen3.8's Groq 200k tokens/day ran out during dev runs, and gpt-oss strict json_schema can 400 'does not match the expected schema'.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
